  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Men and women develop sustainable actions to improve access to water for safe drinking and farming</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This project seeks to support rural communities, and develop sustainable actions to alleviate water scarcity and improve food security in Altiplano, Bolivia.

Rural communities in the Altiplano suffer from scarcity and contamination of water, which has led to a decreased productivity of land and insufficient access to safe drinking water. 

Component one of the programme will address water resource management issues in communities affected by mining operations and climate change, and component two will tackle issues related to access, sanitation and hygiene. As a whole, the programme seeks to strengthen the capacity of rural and semi-urban communities to manage water resources by making accessible to them technologies and tools, and building their capacity to manage and preserve the vital water resources needed to guarantee food security. 

This means that it will look at water balance, both in terms of water quality and quantity within a geographical water catchment, taking into account ground and surface water, weather and climate issues, as well as a user/stakeholder approach (domestic and urban water use, mining, agriculture, industry).</narrative>
  </description>
